WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/dashboard/components/LayoutSwitcher.tsx — a compact dropdown to switch saved dashboard
  layouts. Pure/presentational (owns no data): props = dashboards, activeId, dirty?, editMode?, onSwitch,
  onCreate→id?, onDuplicate?, onReset, onToggleEdit?, onPinToVehicle?(id, vehicleId). Hooks: useTranslation
  ('dashboard'), useSelectedVehicle()→{vehicleId, vehicle}, useConfirm().
  Branches reproduced (every one):
    • active   = dashboards.find(id===activeId) ?? dashboards[0]
    • visible  = scope==null ? true : (selectedVehicleId!=null && scope===selectedVehicleId)
    • handleSaveAs : blank ⇒ no-op; (onDuplicate && active) ⇒ duplicate(active.id) [typed name ignored];
                     else create(trimmed); suggestion = "${active.name} (Copy)" / "New Layout"
    • handleReset  : useConfirm(danger) → onReset
    • handlePinToggle : active.vehicleId!=null ⇒ unpin(null); else selectedVehicleId!=null ⇒ pin(selected);
                        disabled when active.vehicleId==null && selectedVehicleId==null
    • activeName   = active?.name ?? "Untitled"
    • pinnedLabel  = active?.vehicleId!=null && vehicle ? (display_name ?? vin ?? "#id") : null
    • trigger(Layout label + name + dirty badge + pinned badge + chevron) + inline Edit/SaveAs/Reset (sm:flex)
    • menu(radio rows: name + default badge + pin glyph + active check; empty line; New-from-current; pin
      toggle; Reset(danger); footer hint)

