PARITY MAPPING (web → Apple platform tokens; no Tailwind/DOM ported)
  custom dropdown + click-outside/Escape handlers → native .popover (self-dismissing, HIG) with
      .presentationCompactAdaptation(.popover) so iPhone shows a popover, not a sheet.
  useConfirm danger dialog                         → native .alert (destructive Reset + Cancel).
  window.prompt save-as                            → native .alert with a TextField (+ Save / Cancel).
  useSelectedVehicle / useTranslation              → injected into LayoutSwitcherData + LayoutSwitcherLocalizer
                                                     (parent maps the S8 holders; the view does ZERO I/O — web parity).
  Badge / Button / chevron / icons                 → LayoutChip (TSTone tokens) · TSButton(.ghost,.small) ·
                                                     SF Symbols (chevron.down, pin.fill, checkmark, plus,
                                                     arrow.counterclockwise, pin.slash, square.and.arrow.down).
  Tailwind colors/spacing/radius                   → Color.TS.* / TSSpacing / TSRadius (generated tokens).
  i18n   : every string via LayoutSwitcherStrings/.echo — zero English literals in code paths; the 23 web
           t()-keys are preserved verbatim (layout.* + common.cancel) so a shared catalog resolves identically.
  a11y   : trigger = button w/ label "Switch dashboard layout" + value = composed selection; rows carry
           name/default/pinned/selected VoiceOver tags + .isSelected; toolbar buttons labelled; reduce-motion
           respected by the shared TSSkeleton; Dynamic Type via the Font.TS ramp.
  telemetry : view.opened surface="LayoutSwitcher" via LayoutSwitcherSurface.reportOpen (P1/S11), default OSLog sink.

STATES (every state renders — verified by previews + the loaded/empty/error/loading/stale/offline branches)
  loading → skeleton trigger · empty → friendly "No saved layouts" trigger · error → message + Retry ·
  loaded → full switcher · stale/offline → the loaded switcher with a stale/offline freshness chip on the trigger
  (the collection is never hidden behind a null check).

